    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1380">

                <pb facs="1351" n="1341" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.91/9–1649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-16T09:00:00+09:00">September 16,
                            1949—9 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 15—10:31 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>480. ReContel 479, September 15. K. C. Wu called last night several hours after
                    my visit to him and said he saw Governor Chen and had him telephone Admiral
                    Kwei, now South Taiwan, to use his influence our behalf. Governor told Wu he in
                    sympathy our request and telegraphed Minister National Defense following my
                    visit. Wu and Wang Shih-chieh<anchor n="65" xml:id="d1380-f1"/> sent joint
                    telegram Foreign Office as representatives Generalissimo’s headquarters strongly
                    recommending that American <pb facs="1352" n="1342" xml:id="pg1342"/> proposals
                    be accepted. Generalissimo still Chengtu, otherwise Wu would have approached
                    him.</p>
                <p>Department may wish pass this information Embassy office Canton.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1380-f1" n="65" xml:id="d1380-f1-content">
                <p>Former Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
